From f4e0585564beec2ba4ddf21fe0f7fb845b3f1b92 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Polari Suite <polari@localhost.invalid>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:54:21 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] hw/misc: polari-block, a register block driven by a
 Polari device layout; esp32c3 polari-layout property

pt-1b (Polari PIN_TWIN_PLAN.md). -machine esp32c3,polari-layout=FILE creates polari-block, which maps only the
layout's register runs at priority 1 over the vendor regions (esp32.gpio, the esp32c3.iomem catch-all), so
every other offset falls through unchanged. Writes are interpreted by each field's access word; a w1-set /
w1-clear field acts on the register its row names. -global polari-block.dump=FILE writes the final register
state at exit. Its IRQ line is wired to ETS_GPIO_INTR_SOURCE (not raised until pt-3). Unset: the stock path.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
